WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.166 --> 00:00:01.601
360 exclusive inside

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:02.702
the fighting in Ukraine

00:00:02.702 --> 00:00:03.737
from a perspective

00:00:03.737 --> 00:00:05.405
that's never been shown before.

00:00:05.405 --> 00:00:07.607
The view from inside a Ukrainian combat

00:00:07.607 --> 00:00:09.676
helicopter flying at treetop level

00:00:09.676 --> 00:00:11.778
and sometimes below the tree line

00:00:11.778 --> 00:00:13.279
under constant threat from ground

00:00:13.279 --> 00:00:14.848
fire and fighters above.

00:00:14.848 --> 00:00:15.348
Flying

00:00:15.348 --> 00:00:16.082
these choppers

00:00:16.082 --> 00:00:17.851
is one of the most dangerous jobs

00:00:17.851 --> 00:00:19.052
in this war.

00:00:19.052 --> 00:00:19.686
And with Russia

00:00:19.686 --> 00:00:20.787
beginning a new offensive,

00:00:20.787 --> 00:00:22.455
it could soon get even riskier.

00:00:22.455 --> 00:00:25.692
CNN Sam Kiley has the story.

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:28.828
The target is

00:00:28.828 --> 00:00:30.630
Russian troops

00:00:37.837 --> 00:00:39.139
a hard bank left

00:00:39.139 --> 00:00:40.640
and a dove

00:00:41.975 --> 00:00:43.343
and flares to distract

00:00:43.343 --> 00:00:45.812
Heat-Seeking missiles.

00:00:47.614 --> 00:00:49.816
A pair of Ukrainian helicopters

00:00:49.816 --> 00:00:51.885
on an assault against Russian forces

00:00:52.152 --> 00:00:54.320
close to parliament.

00:00:54.754 --> 00:00:57.123
Russian aircraft

00:00:57.123 --> 00:00:59.225
are raging around the border.

00:00:59.225 --> 00:01:00.560
It's on the front line.

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:02.162
You should be careful

00:01:02.162 --> 00:01:03.463
when you go watch a flight

00:01:03.463 --> 00:01:05.932
from very low altitude and very low speed

00:01:07.167 --> 00:01:08.201
to prevent

00:01:08.201 --> 00:01:10.603
to prevent our recognition

00:01:12.672 --> 00:01:15.041
below trenches.

00:01:15.041 --> 00:01:15.508
And east

00:01:15.508 --> 00:01:17.777
Ukrainian villages smashed by war

00:01:19.646 --> 00:01:20.246
just

00:01:23.716 --> 00:01:25.051
back from the sortie.

00:01:25.051 --> 00:01:27.187
This forward base is secret,

00:01:27.187 --> 00:01:29.923
as low profile as possible.

00:01:29.923 --> 00:01:32.092
The eight helicopters are refueled

00:01:32.826 --> 00:01:34.194
and rearmed.

00:01:34.194 --> 00:01:36.496
They expect to fly at least three sorties

00:01:36.496 --> 00:01:37.864
a day.

00:01:38.131 --> 00:01:39.532
When you took off this morning,

00:01:39.532 --> 00:01:41.801
were you frightened by

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:44.971
Well, because the Russians

00:01:44.971 --> 00:01:46.339
want to kill you.

00:01:46.339 --> 00:01:48.108
So they don't have any other choice

00:01:48.108 --> 00:01:50.376
than to fight the Russians.

00:01:50.577 --> 00:01:53.213
If you frightened, should stay at home.

00:01:53.346 --> 00:01:55.949
That's not an option here.

00:01:57.584 --> 00:01:58.218
This Soviet

00:01:58.218 --> 00:02:01.020
era helicopter is about 30 years old.

00:02:01.254 --> 00:02:03.323
The threat against it is extreme.

00:02:03.323 --> 00:02:04.757
And as a result of that,

00:02:04.757 --> 00:02:06.259
we're having to fly

00:02:06.259 --> 00:02:08.128
quite literally below

00:02:08.128 --> 00:02:09.863
the height of trees,

00:02:09.863 --> 00:02:13.333
climbing and chipping with every piece of

00:02:13.333 --> 00:02:14.667
woodland that we pass.

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:18.805
Built as transport aircraft.

00:02:18.805 --> 00:02:19.806
They're most vulnerable

00:02:19.806 --> 00:02:22.008
when they climb to shoot their rockets,

00:02:23.343 --> 00:02:25.278
diving for cover to 20 feet above

00:02:25.278 --> 00:02:27.380
the ground is also perilous.

00:02:31.518 --> 00:02:32.886
A change in sound

00:02:32.886 --> 00:02:34.354
indicates a tree strike

00:02:34.354 --> 00:02:37.357
by the helicopter's blades

00:02:39.392 --> 00:02:40.093
Back at base,

00:02:40.093 --> 00:02:41.861
the blades are swapped quickly.

00:02:41.861 --> 00:02:44.130
Ukraine doesn't have aircraft to spare.

00:02:45.498 --> 00:02:45.932
This

00:02:47.167 --> 00:02:49.102
no pilots, sir.

00:02:49.102 --> 00:02:50.170
He skippers the chopper

00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:52.205
that hit the trees

00:02:52.205 --> 00:02:53.773
in year of routine.

00:02:53.773 --> 00:02:55.441
He tells me in December,

00:02:55.441 --> 00:02:57.377
a very close friend of mine died.

00:02:57.377 --> 00:02:58.111
A lot of people

00:02:58.111 --> 00:02:58.511
I knew

00:02:58.511 --> 00:03:00.780
friends have already died, unfortunately.

00:03:01.381 --> 00:03:03.550
It's very painful and I'm very upset

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:05.451
and I cannot move on.

00:03:05.451 --> 00:03:07.053
We're supposed to.

00:03:07.053 --> 00:03:08.221
He went on.

00:03:08.221 --> 00:03:10.857
We need new attack helicopters, new jets.

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:12.792
Unfortunately, our equipment is old

00:03:12.792 --> 00:03:14.661
and its range is very small,

00:03:14.661 --> 00:03:15.962
and it's inaccurate.

00:03:18.565 --> 00:03:20.667
A year into fighting Russia's invasion,

00:03:20.934 --> 00:03:23.703
Ukraine is still asking for more advanced

00:03:23.703 --> 00:03:25.471
helicopters and jets.

00:03:25.471 --> 00:03:26.973
So far, the response from her

00:03:26.973 --> 00:03:29.943
allies has been sorry, but no.

00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:33.046
And so they fight on here with what

00:03:33.046 --> 00:03:34.180
they've got

00:03:38.418 --> 00:03:40.587
Kylie joins us now from eastern Ukraine.

00:03:40.587 --> 00:03:42.555
That's incredible.

00:03:42.589 --> 00:03:44.490
What was it like in that helicopter?

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:44.924
I mean,

00:03:45.225 --> 00:03:46.559
the idea that you're flying below

00:03:46.559 --> 00:03:46.993
the tree

00:03:46.993 --> 00:03:47.560
line,

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:49.596
that the rotor of the helicopter

00:03:49.596 --> 00:03:50.897
actually hit a tree?

00:03:50.897 --> 00:03:51.965
I mean, it's extraordinary

00:03:51.965 --> 00:03:55.168
the risk that these pilots are taking

00:03:56.836 --> 00:03:58.238
It is extraordinary risk.

00:03:58.238 --> 00:04:00.440
It's a real sad David and Goliath.

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:02.909
If we needed one of those comparisons

00:04:02.909 --> 00:04:04.677
in Ukraine, that would be it.

00:04:04.677 --> 00:04:06.512
These are ancient helicopters,

00:04:06.512 --> 00:04:07.380
that sort of

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:09.282
Soviet equivalent of a Black Hawk,

00:04:09.282 --> 00:04:11.184
but a very old and ancient

00:04:11.184 --> 00:04:13.319
Blackhawk transport helicopter fitted

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:15.888
with these rocket pods

00:04:15.888 --> 00:04:19.125
and sent into battle of fearful

00:04:19.125 --> 00:04:20.460
of fighter

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:21.427
jets, of surface

00:04:21.427 --> 00:04:23.596
to air missiles, of ground fire

00:04:23.630 --> 00:04:24.430
I mean, they

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:25.765
and when we were on that aircraft,

00:04:25.765 --> 00:04:27.267
I could have almost leant out the window

00:04:27.267 --> 00:04:28.668
and touched the stubble

00:04:28.668 --> 00:04:30.203
of the trees,

00:04:30.203 --> 00:04:32.538
of the fields of passing below me.

00:04:32.572 --> 00:04:35.441
So it really is extremely high risk.

00:04:35.441 --> 00:04:37.176
They have taken pretty heavy

00:04:37.176 --> 00:04:38.645
casualties, particularly

00:04:38.645 --> 00:04:39.579
at the beginning of the war,

00:04:39.579 --> 00:04:41.748
before they could organize themselves.

00:04:41.781 --> 00:04:42.181
The other thing

00:04:42.181 --> 00:04:43.850
I think is important to note here,

00:04:43.850 --> 00:04:46.786
by fluke entirely by fluke,

00:04:46.786 --> 00:04:48.121
a lot of these veteran pilots

00:04:48.121 --> 00:04:49.389
have been flying

00:04:49.389 --> 00:04:50.823
recently in the last 15,

00:04:50.823 --> 00:04:53.192
20 years on a peacekeeping missions

00:04:53.192 --> 00:04:55.094
with the United Nations in Africa.

00:04:55.094 --> 00:04:56.496
So they've got a lot of hours.

00:04:56.496 --> 00:04:57.630
They've got a lot of hours

00:04:57.630 --> 00:04:58.898
in areas of conflict,

00:04:58.898 --> 00:05:00.700
like the Democratic Republic

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:02.502
of the Congo and Sierra Leone.

00:05:02.502 --> 00:05:05.204
Liberia, Mozambique and elsewhere.

00:05:05.204 --> 00:05:07.340
And as a consequence of that,

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:08.641
they're pretty,

00:05:08.841 --> 00:05:10.243
very, very highly skilled.

00:05:10.243 --> 00:05:11.277
And they're all paired

00:05:11.277 --> 00:05:12.812
with much younger pilots.

00:05:12.812 --> 00:05:14.480
But one of the younger pilots

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:16.582
I spoke to who has been flying in

00:05:16.616 --> 00:05:17.884
just a few years

00:05:17.884 --> 00:05:19.652
this year alone, Anderson,

00:05:19.652 --> 00:05:22.188
he counted to 100 combat sorties

00:05:22.388 --> 00:05:24.691
and then stop bothering Anderson.

00:05:24.691 --> 00:05:25.258
Incredible.

00:05:25.258 --> 00:05:26.759
Sam Kiley, thank you for that report.

00:05:26.759 --> 00:05:27.627
Really extraordinary.

00:05:27.627 --> 00:05:28.661
CNN military

00:05:28.661 --> 00:05:29.495
analyst and retired Army

00:05:29.495 --> 00:05:30.596
Lieutenant General Mark Hertling

00:05:30.596 --> 00:05:31.831
joins us now.

00:05:31.831 --> 00:05:32.432
General Hurley,

00:05:32.432 --> 00:05:33.466
I mean, are those helicopters

00:05:33.466 --> 00:05:35.702
even designed for fear that

00:05:37.303 --> 00:05:37.837
they are?

00:05:37.837 --> 00:05:40.340
Anderson, those are my 17 helicopters.

00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:42.508
I think I just picked it up on the film

00:05:42.508 --> 00:05:44.644
as Sam was doing his report.

00:05:44.644 --> 00:05:46.112
And what what they're flying is

00:05:46.112 --> 00:05:47.747
what's called nap of the Earth.

00:05:47.747 --> 00:05:49.515
All combat aircraft do that.

00:05:49.515 --> 00:05:51.451
They try and stay as low as possible

00:05:51.451 --> 00:05:53.419
to avoid any kind of radar signatures.

00:05:53.419 --> 00:05:55.455
And there is that up and down

00:05:55.455 --> 00:05:56.456
nap of the earth

00:05:56.456 --> 00:05:58.524
under undulating terrain.

00:05:58.524 --> 00:06:00.360
But they are firing rocket pods

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:01.094
and rocket

00:06:01.094 --> 00:06:02.762
pods are not precision weapons.

00:06:02.762 --> 00:06:03.496
They're are somewhat

00:06:03.496 --> 00:06:05.098
the artillery of the air.

00:06:05.098 --> 00:06:06.366
So it's difficult

00:06:06.366 --> 00:06:08.401
to really get a target strike with that

00:06:08.401 --> 00:06:09.235
unless you're

00:06:09.235 --> 00:06:11.070
literally pointing at the target.

00:06:11.070 --> 00:06:12.038
And you could see

00:06:12.038 --> 00:06:12.672
the helicopter

00:06:12.672 --> 00:06:14.307
was flying over the terrain.

00:06:14.307 --> 00:06:17.076
And as they just fired their rockets,

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:19.412
they're really aiming toward an area

00:06:19.412 --> 00:06:21.848
for an area fire versus a precise target.

00:06:22.014 --> 00:06:23.750
So what would more advanced

00:06:23.750 --> 00:06:26.285
aircraft, advanced helicopters or,

00:06:26.285 --> 00:06:26.753
you know,

00:06:27.887 --> 00:06:30.923
helicopter gunships or aircraft?

00:06:31.124 --> 00:06:32.158
What would that allow

00:06:32.158 --> 00:06:35.294
Ukrainian forces to do that they can't?

00:06:35.294 --> 00:06:37.296
Well, in some cases,

00:06:37.530 --> 00:06:38.598
certainly they

00:06:38.598 --> 00:06:40.533
advanced Western style aircraft.

00:06:40.533 --> 00:06:42.568
Sam mentioned the Black Hawk.

00:06:42.568 --> 00:06:44.203
I kind of chafed a little bit

00:06:44.203 --> 00:06:46.472
when you said they're Asian ancient

00:06:46.472 --> 00:06:47.974
because they are not ancient.

00:06:47.974 --> 00:06:49.642
They're actually pretty new

00:06:49.642 --> 00:06:50.943
in the Army's imagery.

00:06:50.943 --> 00:06:53.012
But it will allow them more transport.

00:06:53.012 --> 00:06:54.881
It would give them guns on the side,

00:06:54.881 --> 00:06:56.315
the same kind of rocket pods

00:06:56.315 --> 00:06:56.949
where I think

00:06:56.949 --> 00:06:58.684
the pilots you're talking about

00:06:58.684 --> 00:07:00.553
are more the attack helicopters.

00:07:00.553 --> 00:07:02.889
Like Apaches or even Cobras.

00:07:03.356 --> 00:07:05.725
Those are extremely expensive,

00:07:05.725 --> 00:07:07.493
very technologically advanced,

00:07:07.493 --> 00:07:09.262
takes a whole lot of training

00:07:09.262 --> 00:07:10.430
and a whole lot of maintenance.

00:07:10.430 --> 00:07:12.598
But they fire precision weapons

00:07:13.499 --> 00:07:14.434
from the aircraft

00:07:14.434 --> 00:07:15.868
and they can be tank killers

00:07:15.868 --> 00:07:16.969
from literally

00:07:17.970 --> 00:07:20.173
almost up to 12 kilometers away.

00:07:20.173 --> 00:07:21.274
But the training on that,

00:07:21.274 --> 00:07:23.876
how long does that take?

00:07:23.876 --> 00:07:24.811
It's immense.

00:07:24.811 --> 00:07:25.411
You know,

00:07:25.545 --> 00:07:28.981
there's been talk a lot about the F-16s.

00:07:29.515 --> 00:07:30.516
You would probably have

00:07:30.516 --> 00:07:32.218
to put as much time

00:07:32.218 --> 00:07:34.320
in an Apache helicopters

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:36.322
you would for an F-16.

00:07:36.322 --> 00:07:36.889
And there's,

00:07:36.889 --> 00:07:37.190
you know,

00:07:37.190 --> 00:07:37.924
a lot of language saying

00:07:37.924 --> 00:07:39.392
we need to give them the F-16.

00:07:39.392 --> 00:07:39.959
You're in

00:07:39.959 --> 00:07:41.828
ad who's the spokesman for the Ukrainian

00:07:41.828 --> 00:07:42.562
Air Force,

00:07:42.562 --> 00:07:43.563
just said last week

00:07:43.563 --> 00:07:44.130
that it would take

00:07:44.130 --> 00:07:45.398
Ukrainian pilots

00:07:45.398 --> 00:07:46.466
a couple of weeks

00:07:46.466 --> 00:07:49.001
to just learn how to fly fighter jets.

00:07:49.235 --> 00:07:51.270
But about six months to really master

00:07:51.270 --> 00:07:52.705
how to fight the aircraft.

00:07:52.705 --> 00:07:54.307
That's about the same

00:07:54.307 --> 00:07:55.842
for an Apache helicopter

00:07:55.842 --> 00:07:56.843
because they are

00:07:56.843 --> 00:07:58.811
so technologically advanced.

00:07:58.811 --> 00:08:00.346
They have heads up displays

00:08:00.346 --> 00:08:02.048
on their helmets themselves.

00:08:02.048 --> 00:08:03.683
Takes two pilots

00:08:03.683 --> 00:08:05.818
and it would just really take a very long

00:08:05.852 --> 00:08:06.853
training time

00:08:06.853 --> 00:08:08.955
besides being extremely expensive.

00:08:08.955 --> 00:08:10.022
General Hurtling, I appreciate it.

00:08:10.022 --> 00:08:10.423
Thank you.

